{"architectures":["x64"],"id":"ZeroClawLabs.ZeroClaw","latestVersion":"0.9.0","media":{"icons":[],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"copyright":"© 2026 ZeroClaw Labs. All rights reserved.","description":"Fast, small, and fully autonomous AI assistant framework — deploy anywhere, swap anything 🦀","documentations":[{"DocumentLabel":"Documentation","DocumentUrl":"https://www.zeroclawlabs.ai/docs"}],"license":"MIT or Apache-2.0","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw#license","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"copyright":"© 2026 ZeroClaw Labs. All rights reserved.","description":"Fast, small, and fully autonomous AI assistant framework — deploy anywhere, swap anything 🦀","documentations":[{"DocumentLabel":"Documentation","DocumentUrl":"https://www.zeroclawlabs.ai/docs"}],"license":"MIT or Apache-2.0","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw#license","locale":"en-US","longDescription":"ZeroClaw is the runtime framework for agentic workflows — infrastructure that abstracts models, tools, memory, and execution so agents can be built once and run anywhere.\n✨ Features\n- 🏎️ Lean Runtime by Default: Common CLI and status workflows run in a few-megabyte memory envelope on release builds.\n- 💰 Cost-Efficient Deployment: Designed for low-cost boards and small cloud instances without heavyweight runtime dependencies.\n- ⚡ Fast Cold Starts: Single-binary Rust runtime keeps command and daemon startup near-instant for daily operations.\n- 🌍 Portable Architecture: One binary-first workflow across ARM, x86, and RISC-V with swappable providers/channels/tools.\n- 🔍 Research Phase: Proactive information gathering through tools before response generation — reduces hallucinations by fact-checking first.\nWhy teams pick ZeroClaw\n- Lean by default: small Rust binary, fast startup, low memory footprint.\n- Secure by design: pairing, strict sandboxing, explicit allowlists, workspace scoping.\n- Fully swappable: core systems are traits (providers, channels, tools, memory, tunnels).\n- No lock-in: OpenAI-compatible provider support + pluggable custom endpoints.","name":"ZeroClaw","packageUrl":"https://www.zeroclawlabs.ai/","publisher":"ZeroClaw Labs","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw/issues","publisherUrl":"https://www.zeroclawlabs.ai/","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw/releases/tag/v0.9.0","tags":["agent","agentic","ai","chatbot","claw","large-language-model","llm"]},"zh-CN":{"description":"快速、小巧且完全自主的 AI 助手框架——可部署于任意位置，随意替换任何组件 🦀","documentations":[{"DocumentLabel":"文档","DocumentUrl":"https://www.zeroclawlabs.ai/docs"}],"locale":"zh-CN","longDescription":"ZeroClaw 是用于智能体工作流的运行时框架——一种抽象了模型、工具、记忆和执行的基础设施，使智能体能够一次构建，随处运行。\n✨ 特性\n- 🏎️ 默认轻量运行时：常见的 CLI 和状态工作流在发布版本中仅占用几兆内存。\n- 💰 成本高效的部署：专为低成本开发板和小型云实例设计，无需沉重的运行时依赖。\n- ⚡ 极快的冷启动：单一二进制的 Rust 运行时，使命令和守护进程的启动接近瞬间完成，适合日常操作。\n- 🌍 可移植架构：支持 ARM、x86 和 RISC-V 的单一二进制优先工作流，支持可替换的供应商/通道/工具。\n- 🔍 研究阶段：在生成响应之前，通过工具主动收集信息——通过先行事实核查减少幻觉。\n团队选择 ZeroClaw 的原因\n- 默认轻量：小巧的 Rust 二进制文件，快速启动，低内存占用。\n- 设计安全：配对机制、严格沙箱、明确的允许列表、工作区范围限制。\n- 完全可替换：核心系统均为 trait（供应商、通道、工具、记忆、隧道）。\n- 无厂商锁定：支持兼容 OpenAI 的供应商，以及可插拔的自定义端点。","tags":["人工智能","大语言模型","智能体","聊天机器人","自主智能","龙虾"]}},"longDescription":"ZeroClaw is the runtime framework for agentic workflows — infrastructure that abstracts models, tools, memory, and execution so agents can be built once and run anywhere.\n✨ Features\n- 🏎️ Lean Runtime by Default: Common CLI and status workflows run in a few-megabyte memory envelope on release builds.\n- 💰 Cost-Efficient Deployment: Designed for low-cost boards and small cloud instances without heavyweight runtime dependencies.\n- ⚡ Fast Cold Starts: Single-binary Rust runtime keeps command and daemon startup near-instant for daily operations.\n- 🌍 Portable Architecture: One binary-first workflow across ARM, x86, and RISC-V with swappable providers/channels/tools.\n- 🔍 Research Phase: Proactive information gathering through tools before response generation — reduces hallucinations by fact-checking first.\nWhy teams pick ZeroClaw\n- Lean by default: small Rust binary, fast startup, low memory footprint.\n- Secure by design: pairing, strict sandboxing, explicit allowlists, workspace scoping.\n- Fully swappable: core systems are traits (providers, channels, tools, memory, tunnels).\n- No lock-in: OpenAI-compatible provider support + pluggable custom endpoints.","name":"ZeroClaw","packageUrl":"https://www.zeroclawlabs.ai/","publisher":"ZeroClaw Labs","publisherSupportUrl":"https://github.com/zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw/issues","publisherUrl":"https://www.zeroclawlabs.ai/","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/zeroclaw-labs/zeroclaw/releases/tag/v0.9.0","tags":["agent","agentic","ai","chatbot","claw","large-language-model","llm"]},"schemaVersion":1,"source":"winget","versions":[{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/0.9.0/app.json","detailSha256":"c12a256a0f8c8befd4292cada704fa076acfd3d191ce69d64e070abc6632965f","releaseDate":"2026-11-12","releaseDateSource":"commit","version":"0.9.0"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/0.8.7/app.json","detailSha256":"3bca6af292bf333f3f61149fbc101af522b7b90c63140022d8fb6ad2e2f9c60c","releaseDate":"2026-10-27","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"0.8.7"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/0.8.6/app.json","detailSha256":"e312dcc6cd73340ce7e403ae7f2ec1d835b8370ef72b757868fd3f9251aabf0f","releaseDate":"2026-10-18","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"0.8.6"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/0.8.5/app.json","detailSha256":"12c9bb1ae8e5f58fec1a9f940815b3907a0f7a90a1ea23756337fd4120a87368","releaseDate":"2026-09-05","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"0.8.5"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/0.8.4/app.json","detailSha256":"2fbf0a323b0aafce42c9e2dcc7ce9ba396653f653b9376657a37ab8d5e409e73","releaseDate":"2026-08-02","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"0.8.4"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/0.8.3/app.json","det